/*!
\page page_strichpixel StRichPixel

\brief \ref page_strichpixel "StRichPixel" — raw RICH pad pixel with bit-packed row, column, and ADC data.

\section strichpixel_overview Overview
StRichPixel stores a single raw pad signal from the RICH cathode pad plane.
It is the lowest-level data object in the RICH reconstruction chain. The pad
plane is organised in rows and columns; the ADC value is 10-bit (0–1023) with
an overflow sentinel at 1024. All three quantities are packed into a single
\c UInt_t to minimise memory footprint.

\section strichpixel_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StRichPixel
\endcode

\section strichpixel_members Data Members
| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| UInt_t | mPackedData | Bit-packed: bits[7:0]=pad, bits[15:8]=row, bits[26:16]=ADC (bit 26 = overflow flag) |

\section strichpixel_methods Key Methods
| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| int pad() const | Pad (column) index from bits [7:0] |
| int row() const | Row index from bits [15:8] |
| int adc() const | ADC value; 1024 if overflow flag is set |
| void setPackedData(unsigned int) | Set the entire packed word |

\section strichpixel_related Related Classes
\ref page_strichmcpixel "StRichMCPixel" extends this class with Monte Carlo truth.
See also \ref page_strichcollection "StRichCollection" for the container that holds pixel vectors.
*/
